# AfriCup Backyard Challenge — environment variables
#
# The app works WITHOUT any of these: with no env vars it runs in single-device
# localStorage mode (zero config, great for one phone / one laptop at the party).
#
# Fill these in to auto-upgrade to LIVE multi-phone sync (free Supabase tier).
# 1. Create a free project at https://supabase.com
# 2. Run supabase/schema.sql in the project's SQL editor
# 3. Copy this file to ".env", paste the values below, then restart `npm run dev`
#
# Find both values in your Supabase dashboard under: Project Settings → API.

# Your project URL, e.g. https://abcdefghijklmno.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The "anon" / public API key (safe to expose in a client app).
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
